{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20318",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.15,
      "end_seconds": 5.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, um, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.21,
      "end_seconds": 15.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Alright, you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.02,
      "end_seconds": 24.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got pain going down the back of my left leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.29,
      "end_seconds": 27.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.71,
      "end_seconds": 31.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "It's been two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.44,
      "end_seconds": 35.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.85,
      "end_seconds": 56.88,
      "duration_seconds": 20.03,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get lower back pain as well. The lower back pain? That's been for nearly five years. About lower back pain, I'd give it a six, out of ten. Bending definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.48,
      "end_seconds": 66.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Have you had pain going down the back of your left leg before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.62,
      "end_seconds": 76.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.36,
      "end_seconds": 82.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Any fever, numbness between the legs, weight loss or bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.44,
      "end_seconds": 92.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Uh, no, no fever, numbness between the legs, weight loss or bladder problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.5,
      "end_seconds": 95.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.08,
      "end_seconds": 99.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.68,
      "end_seconds": 104.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.29,
      "end_seconds": 108.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.62,
      "end_seconds": 112.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.5,
      "end_seconds": 120.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I take valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day. Paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.16,
      "end_seconds": 138.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.52,
      "end_seconds": 142.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.54,
      "end_seconds": 155.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.34,
      "end_seconds": 169.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about ten years. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.58,
      "end_seconds": 178.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.04,
      "end_seconds": 182.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No surgery, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.9,
      "end_seconds": 188.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.7,
      "end_seconds": 209.27,
      "duration_seconds": 18.57,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I hardly move around during the day. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.14,
      "end_seconds": 215.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.28,
      "end_seconds": 228.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.34,
      "end_seconds": 256.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 72 beats a minute, pressure 109 over 76, saturation 98 percent, temperature is 36.4 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.35,
      "end_seconds": 260.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Erm, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.09,
      "end_seconds": 265.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.12,
      "end_seconds": 271.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.37,
      "end_seconds": 274.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.22,
      "end_seconds": 277.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.07,
      "end_seconds": 295.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Straight leg raising on the left brings on the leg pain at about forty degrees, and the power and reflexes are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.19,
      "end_seconds": 331.87,
      "duration_seconds": 32.68,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably sciatica from a lumbar disc irritation. We should do an MRI of the lower back for sciatica. I'm going to order blood tests, for back pain. We'll begin with naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, for one week. You take it by mouth. That's for back and leg pain. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.05,
      "end_seconds": 363.19,
      "duration_seconds": 30.14,
      "text": "Stay active and keep walking, bed rest makes this slower to settle. I'd like you to see physiotherapy as well, and I'll write the referral. The thing that would worry me is if you get numbness between the legs or trouble passing urine. If that happens, go to emergency. Book a review after the scan. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.07,
      "end_seconds": 369.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Right, um, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.81,
      "end_seconds": 372.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}